% The exact program from the Scheme-backend performance report: a
% non-tail-recursive user function whose generated code used to be
% dominated by one `call/cc` escape per recursion level (and one per
% prelude arithmetic/comparison helper it called). The codegen unit test
% pins the generated shape; this case pins the semantics on both
% backends end to end.
:- module(user_sum, [compute/2, fun sum/1]).
:- chr_constraint compute(int, int).
:- function sum(int) -> int.

sum(0) -> 0.
sum(N) | N > 0 -> N + sum(N - 1).

compute(N, R) <=> R is sum(N).
